+# GDE1 bounded native qualification
+
+This is an opt-in CPU research admission for local outcome-modulated decoder
+plasticity. It is not a trained brain, recurrent BPTT, a default-game/GPU feature,
+a migration, or evidence of improved survival or avoidance. The separate
+six-weight taste-reference repair and scientific recovery study are excluded.
+
+## Frozen scope and evidence
+
+The tested code is `ed5f2f5a13e9d7b3851272adeeec7c73b605f7aa`, based on closed host
+`fbf2a517f93098b5d936878a3d26bbb8d0391c38`. The law and inherited rates did not
+change during qualification. Only ActionCandidate/MemoryContext fast and
+eligibility coordinates can evolve. All lifetime, other source banks,
+dendritic/structural state, optimizer moments/ages and 814 appendage rows remain
+closed. See [the design and iteration record](DESIGN.md) for the formula,
+provenance contract and accounting semantics.
+
+Fresh fixtures use the existing fixed seed `0x03475250484F5354`, ordinary
+240- or 1,200-tick preparations, and a maximum of 24 native intervals. No action,
+concentration, coefficient or seed was adjusted to obtain a desired result.
+Finite-difference and explicit zero/opposite-credit tests are synthetic
+mathematical controls, not evidence of lived learning.
+
+The local qualification packet retains initial and final binaries, logs, exact
+wire outputs, numerical diagnostics and real sealed patches. It is separate from
+the source repository; no checkpoint is published with these notes. The initial
+source, source-review corrections, numerical failure and later test revisions
+remain separate commits.
+
+## Measured outcome association
+
+The first update changed 144 fast coordinates and 142 effective weights, but
+its actual sampled joint log probability was **bit-identical** in a detached
+same-frame replay. Raw component change reached `9.0013998e-8`, survived into M2
+port activations at `2.98023224e-8`, then rounded away by the bounded final
+readout. The original failing assertion and binary are retained, not erased.
+
+At representative coordinate 28,720: raw gradient `-0.029025819375`, staged
+trace `-0.02902581915`, delayed trace `-0.02757452801`, inherited eta `0.01`,
+alpha `0.1341599822`, receptor projection `-0.00500660250`, fast delta
+`1.85214148e-7`, and effective-weight delta `2.48483261e-8`. No rate/gain was
+changed in response to this scale finding.
+
+On the second interval, at tick 241, the same captured source state, frame,
+recall/context, appendage, mask and sample were replayed with inherited initial
+fast versus acquired fast. Joint log probability changed from
+`-1.72611119307095584` to `-1.72611475035219319` (about `-3.55728e-6`). The
+separate last-update-only contrast also changed. This is a same-frame policy
+effect, not an alternative lived trajectory, changed-action claim or benefit.
+
+The first computational-cost control separates pre-compute energy change
+`-0.000010192394` from full sealed change `-0.00022572279`. Learning cognitive
+debit was `0.00021549001`, versus closed-host debit `0.0001561075`. Thus that
+closed comparison is **not equal-work**. It establishes compute-inclusive
+outcome modulation, not physical meal or isolated relief learning.
+
+An ordinary physical AwakeRest at tick 242 additionally produced measured
+pre-compute fatigue change `-0.13342218` and energy change `-0.000010192394`.
+The sealed energy change was `-0.00022560358` after cognitive debit
+`0.00021551001`. One sealed update changed 264 fast coordinates and advanced
+weight generation 2 to 3. Its sealed modulator included prediction residual
+`0.35057765`, homeostatic improvement `0.018505063`, frustration `0.03`, and
+zero pain/novelty. The complete patch and physical-versus-sealed measurements
+are retained. Recovery dose 1 is not a fatigue delta of 1. This is aggregate
+joint association with concurrent costs, not proof that relief alone caused
+any update. The tick 241 policy contrast and tick 242 relief receipt are
+separate observations.
+
+## Preservation, derivatives and rejection
+
+- Raw pullbacks agree with the diagnostic dense chain and independent finite
+  differences before eligibility clipping, at nonunit temperatures. Cases
+  cover ordinary ActionCandidate, ordinary MemoryContext, common Rest,
+  operation-specific memory, clipped zero slopes, explicit derived vocal lane
+  42, and a masked zero control.
+- Exact owner, frame, selected action, sequence, dispatch, activation side,
+  feature, phenotype, source-weight generation and source biochemical frame
+  checks reject mismatches. Duplicate credit, cross-policy restore, pending
+  export and a late failing host step are covered. Pre-update sampled scores
+  remain intact after fast writes.
+- Acquired fast/eligibility survive actual BodySleep, one canonical memory-only
+  consolidation, exact cold restore, Waking and resumed decisions. Synaptic
+  sleep remains closed and does not create a fake source weight generation.
+- A separately labeled synthetic-sentinel test preserves nonzero recurrent
+  fast/lifetime/eligibility, dendrites, structural edges and optimizer moments
+  and integer ages across warm and exact cold continuation.
+
+## Checks and limits
+
+[Curated scalar results](VALIDATION-SCALARS.json) record exact pass, failure,
+ignore and filtered counts without captured state or raw logs. The selected
+packet covers 93 distinct candidate test cases, including the explicitly run
+normally ignored witness; repeated runs are not independent experiments.
+
+The serial packet passed 11 focused GDE1 tests, plus the added nonzero-bank
+preservation test. The strengthened physical-modulator test passed again on
+the final binary. The 11-test packet was run on `8f4cb562f`; subsequent source
+changes are only the extra test and test-only evidence export, with production
+behavior unchanged. Final-code strict library/tests Clippy passed.
+
+Affected compatibility passed 10 grouped-host tests, two closed Food tests,
+50 mediation tests (46 existing and four new derivative tests), nine M0 tests,
+nine actual M1 host tests, three M1 replay tests, and the literal pre-adapter
+JSON-wire integration test. These categories overlap the four derivative
+cases in the focused packet; do not add their counts as distinct tests. The
+initial M1 filter matched zero tests and is not counted. Existing Food tests
+are compatibility evidence, not harmful-food learning evidence.
+
+Strict `--lib --tests` Clippy passed with `-D warnings`. The expanded
+`--all-targets` attempt did not pass: unchanged example support
+`examples/support/grounded_drive_basis.rs`, through `probe_grounded_drive_basis`,
+has pre-existing dead-code warnings. No full-workspace/GPU validation or
+scientific learning study is claimed.
+
+## Closed baseline witness
+
+The source-identical ignored witness uses the existing closed fixture, exports
+its complete initial envelope, steps at temperatures 0.73 and 1.17, exports both
+full next-step decision tuples and envelopes, and requires exact cold restore
+after each step. The witness source SHA-256 is
+`93e26a73aa733b268786737e2f7bd4d75bd449f122b5716e5dfa20cb9ff65b57`.
+The baseline checkout contains only this test and its module declaration over
+`fbf2a517`; it has no production edits.
+
+Both runs passed and all five output files are byte-identical: 7,116,876 bytes
+per revision, comprising the complete initial envelope, two complete later
+envelopes, and both next-step decision tuples. This is exact byte comparison,
+not a tolerance or activation-only comparison. Binary SHA-256 values:
+
+- Candidate: `2293871f199df17b9c429786f8cd3b475189a95664e756e49ef9eaff4298cda0`.
+- Baseline: `62eb7f9628cfbd8901f9e68ed0c4be42350299c1e4a4331e8fa4388d0992b170`.
+
+Output SHA-256 values:
+
+- Initial envelope: `fe6385e4406ce7e99cbc992d4fbde3d44805835992ea9ad07c02a2c3dc6b8594`.
+- First envelope: `25b61a7550b424a8391c12960ce3b77a3c22b8ad5013cfe2daf8608bce6e56cf`.
+- Second envelope: `cde1d9c9a853402a9af2cf955b359c6d24c3ef34fed7926cd917b0e1f2e30d5c`.
+- First decision: `516d1776531106ba2368242894b1816799e41a84d2e0d54cbbe2c019632e131e`.
+- Second decision: `f8f48d90074f7463c96787074b0b4ac66c814153b70f5dbcc5e16845ffa36275`.
+
+This bounded witness does not prove every possible closed history; the separate
+closed regressions cover additional source, biology and sleep cases. No phase
+timing instrumentation was added: its request arrived after baseline compilation,
+and another build was deliberately avoided.
+
+## Resource boundary
+
+Compilation and tests are serial, using the existing lane 2 target with
+incremental/debug data disabled. No files are deleted. The initial target was
+1,758,545,813 bytes; the 1 GiB growth cap also conservatively includes the
+already-created baseline worktree and retained logs/binaries/witnesses. No
+study seeds, scientific pilot data or active recovery-pair state are touched.
+At native completion the target was 1,758,959,484 bytes, the retained packet
+245,896,162 bytes, and the baseline worktree 156,415,444 bytes. Conservative
+additional growth was 402,725,277 bytes (about 384 MiB), including the baseline
+worktree. The baseline compile, retained binary and output added 80,110,886 bytes
+within its separate 400 MiB sub-budget. Free space was 14,054,305,792 bytes at
+that measurement; concurrent independent work can change it. Small final notes
+and manifest writes add a few kilobytes. Lane 2 was released after all commands
+finished. Further native builds need a fresh coordinator resource allocation.
